        "markdown": "# 🧭 Central Observation\n\nThis specimen is a **hosted guest conversation dominated by Lionel's extended forensic commentary**.\n\nSean supplies the frame, occasional confirmation, laughter, brief prompts, and a late direct question. Lionel supplies most of the episode's argumentative motion.\n\nThe organizing move is not one thesis expanded linearly. It is closer to an **anomaly audit**: Lionel repeatedly takes one evidentiary item, asks what can actually be established, attacks the official interpretation, then moves to the next item. He explicitly casts himself as a trial lawyer/former prosecutor concerned with proof and reasonable doubt. ",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
