          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 2 · Forensic Anomaly Audit\n## 1:27–21:09\n\nLionel adopts the role of defense lawyer and walks item-by-item through the prosecution story: the rifle, DNA, caliber and wound expectations, weapon assembly and scope issues, gunshot-residue questions, the alleged confession, screenshots and authentication, expert commentary, scene handling, and unclear images.   \n\n**Function:** serially test the narrative by asking what each piece of evidence actually proves.\n\n**Recurring move:** `item -> evidentiary question -> analogy or joke -> doubt -> recap -> next item`.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study02-seg3",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "3 · Character and Motive Expansion",
      "root": false,
