        },
        "markdown": "# 5 · Meta-Defense of Inquiry\n## 41:06–45:33\n\nLionel invokes Alex Jones and other controversial narratives, then steps outside the immediate case to explain what he thinks people like Sean, Candace, and himself do: challenge an announced or official storyline. He compares that role with his own past commentary on O.J. Simpson, Casey Anthony, and Trayvon Martin. \n\n**Function:** justify the legitimacy of challenging a narrative before returning to the case.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
