        "markdown": "# 6 · Crowdsourced Evidence Synthesis\n## 45:33–52:47\n\nLionel describes online researchers scrutinizing a vehicle, claimed location evidence, planes, searches, a screwdriver, body-height estimates, and ballistic demonstrations. He treats this distributed “deep diver” activity as a new form of true-crime investigation and argues that the criticism of Candace has displaced discussion of the underlying evidence.  \n\n**Function:** aggregate many small anomalies into a larger picture and elevate the audience/research network into an investigative actor.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
