        "markdown": "# 7 · Opposition and Narrative Tactics\n## 52:47–55:30\n\nLionel moves from case anomalies to a broader account of narrative control, references a CIA document about responses to Warren Commission critics, mentions media relationships, and uses Laura Loomer's repeated criticism of Candace as an example of organized or obsessive opposition. \n\n**Function:** explain why the speaker believes contrary inquiry is attacked rather than answered.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
