      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🧬 Observed Grammar\n\n**host frame -> guest assumes expert role -> serial anomaly audit -> character and motive expansion -> rapport digression -> meta-defense of inquiry -> crowdsourced evidence synthesis -> opposition frame -> host reset question -> qualified answer -> guest signoff -> host-only outro**\n\n**Working format label:** `Hosted Forensic Commentary`\n\nThis is a container-and-performance grammar, not merely a topic sequence.\n\nThe host does relatively little content generation. His structural power comes from **opening the frame, serving as audience surrogate, validating rapport, and eventually forcing a reset with a direct question**.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study02-objects",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Content Objects",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
