      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🎙️ Editorial Moves\n\nCandidate recurring moves visible in this specimen:\n\n- **Assume Expert Role**: Lionel frames himself as lawyer/prosecutor.\n- **Audit Evidence Item**: isolate one claim or object and ask what it proves.\n- **Reenact the Courtroom**: address Sean or an imagined jury to dramatize proof standards.\n- **Analogize for Ridicule or Clarity**: bazooka, lint brush, Nessie, films, food, history.\n- **Recap the Defect**: summarize accumulated doubt before proceeding.\n- **Expand from Evidence to Character/Motive**.\n- **Meta-Frame Inquiry**: explain why challenging official narratives is legitimate.\n- **Aggregate Crowd Research**: treat distributed investigators as a knowledge source.\n- **Qualify Speculation**: mark what remains unknown after exploring possibilities.\n- **Build Rapport**: tease the host and audience while maintaining momentum.\n\nThese are stronger class candidates than the episode's named people or controversies.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study02-interaction",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Host–Guest Interaction",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 850,
        "y": 430
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
