        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🤝 Host–Guest Interaction Pattern\n\nThis transcript is technically conversational but **asymmetrical**.\n\nSean's recurring functions are:\n\n- introduce and authenticate Lionel to the audience\n- name the initial subject\n- provide short answers or laughter\n- act as the hypothetical prosecutor/juror or audience surrogate\n- surface the live chat\n- tolerate and participate in personal banter\n- interrupt late to force one direct question\n- close the guest segment and resume ownership of his own channel\n\nThe most revealing moment comes at 55:30 when Sean says he needs to “squeeze the question in before the hour,” showing how far Lionel has controlled the conversational runway. ",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
