          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🔬 Early Comparison with Study 01\n\n## What repeats\n- Lionel identifies an official or public narrative he distrusts.\n- He decomposes that narrative into mechanisms or claims.\n- He uses historical and pop-cultural analogies heavily.\n- Candace Owens functions as both subject and example of independent inquiry.\n- He repeatedly returns from digression to a larger claim about narrative control.\n- Humor is structural, not incidental.\n\n## What changes\n**Study 01:** one controlled thesis expands through case study, context, synthesis, and audience prescription.\n\n**Study 02:** another host supplies the container; Lionel performs a long serial evidence audit, wanders through character and rapport material, and is eventually pulled back by a host question.\n\nThis argues against one rigid “Lionel episode” template. It favors **shared Lionel move classes plus multiple composition templates**.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study02-absent",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Important Absences and Limits",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 600,
      "height": 500,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
