          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🚫 Important Absences and Limits\n\nThe transcript does not clearly establish that outside video clips are actually played during the appearance, even though Lionel repeatedly describes pictures, video, posts, and other media.\n\nIt also does not show:\n\n- a balanced interview with frequent host questions\n- multiple equal guest voices\n- a tightly timed question-and-answer rhythm\n- a formal source-by-source citation procedure\n- a clean boundary between verified evidence, inference, humor, and speculation\n\nFor Twilite this last point is especially important: future analysis nodes should distinguish **quoted source material**, **speaker claim**, **speaker inference**, **speaker uncertainty**, and **our structural observation** rather than blending them.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lionel-study02-model",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Emerging Template Model",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 700,
        "y": 1040
      },
      "width": 660,
      "height": 540,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
