      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# 🏗️ Emerging Template Model\n\nAfter two specimens, the likely reusable architecture is becoming more layered:\n\n## Shared media/evidence primitives\nVideo Source, Timed Segment, Transcript Segment, Person, Organization, Claim, Evidence Item, Image/Document Source, Uncertainty.\n\n## Lionel move classes\nAudit Evidence, Reenact Proof Test, Identify Pattern, Add Analogy, Recap Defect, Add Context, Meta-Frame Inquiry, Aggregate Research, Qualify Theory, Build Rapport.\n\n## Composition templates\n- **Lionel Thesis Monologue**\n- **Hosted Forensic Commentary**\n- future Media Reaction\n- future Multi-topic Roundup\n- future Interview/Guest Discussion\n\nThe show package may therefore be a **vocabulary plus several grammars**, not a single universal graph.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
    {
