      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "lionel-appearance-grammar-study-02"
        },
        "markdown": "# ➡️ Next Comparison Question\n\nThe next specimen should preferably contain **actual outside media playback**.\n\nWe now have:\n\n- Study 01: standalone thesis monologue\n- Study 02: hosted forensic commentary\n\nWhat we still need to observe is whether a media-reaction episode introduces a genuinely new Lionel move, such as:\n\n**Play Source -> Pause -> Quote/Inspect -> Comment -> Reframe -> Resume Source**\n\nIf that sequence repeats, `Lionel Comments on Media` may indeed deserve a first-class node type with controls over a shared Video Source node.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1786053587115,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
